    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1184">

                <pb facs="1187" n="1021" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg1021"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.504/86</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Ambassador Fletcher to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico City</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-04-27T17:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 27, 1917, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>139. Your telegram No. 131, and in connection with later reports from Tampico, I
                    have received assurances from the acting Minister for Foreign Affairs that the
                    Ministry of War and Marine will be requested at once to order the military
                    commander at Tampico to take immediate steps to protect American life and
                    property.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Fletcher</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
